<rml>
<head>
	<title>Folio idle check</title>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="/folio/folio.rcss"/>
	<style>
		body { background-color: #14141ae8; color: #e8e8f0; font-size: 16dp; padding: 16dp;
		       width: 100%; height: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; }
		h2 { font-size: 13dp; color: #8a8a99; margin: 10dp 0 6dp 0; }
		p { margin-bottom: 6dp; }
		.note { color: #8a8a99; font-size: 13dp; }

		@keyframes pulse {
			from { opacity: 0.2; }
			to   { opacity: 1.0; }
		}
		.pulsing { animation: 1.4s pulse infinite alternate; background-color: #4ec9a0;
		           width: 180dp; height: 32dp; border-radius: 3dp; }

		.fading { background-color: #2b2b36; width: 180dp; height: 32dp; border-radius: 3dp;
		          transition: background-color 0.6s quadratic-in-out; nav: auto; }
		.fading:focus-visible { background-color: #f0c674; }

		input[type="text"] { width: 200dp; padding: 4dp 6dp; nav: auto; background-color: #2b2b36;
		                     color: #e8e8f0; border-radius: 2dp; }
	</style>
</head>
<body>
	<p class="note">Everything here changes with no input, which is what the idle path must not break.
	Run with folio.Invalidation.Trace 1 and watch what it reports.</p>

	<h2>a running animation</h2>
	<div class="pulsing"></div>
	<p class="note">Must report "next update in 0.000s" forever.</p>

	<h2>a caret</h2>
	<input type="text" value="focus me"/>
	<p class="note">Focused, the caret blinks on a timer with no input, so the report must be a small
	delay rather than "never".</p>

	<h2>a transition</h2>
	<div class="fading" tabindex="auto"></div>
	<p class="note">Navigate onto it: the colour must finish moving after the key is released, which
	only happens if the document keeps updating without further input.</p>
</body>
</rml>
